course: dictionary
lesson: 5236
title: Jewel: a stone, a treasure, or a star
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A jewel is a precious stone, such as a diamond, ruby or emerald, often cut so that it shines. A jewel can also be a piece of jewellery that has such a stone in it, like a ring or a crown.
explain: The word can also mean someone or something very special and valuable. «She is a jewel» does not mean she is made of stone. To check, put the stone meaning into the sentence: "She is a precious stone" makes no sense, so the special-person meaning must be right.
explain: Look at the words around jewel to decide which meaning it has. Pirates hiding jewels in a chest means real stones, and «the jewel of the city» means the best thing in the city.
fact: A jewel is a precious stone, such as a diamond, ruby or emerald, often cut to shine.
fact: «Jewels» are often set in crowns, rings and necklaces.
fact: In science, jewels are gemstones dug out of the ground.
fact: «Jewel in the crown» means the best part of something.
fact: Caddis fly larvae glue sand grains and tiny shells together to make a case; an artist gave them gold flakes and pearls, and «they made jewel cases», cases that sparkled like little jewels.
exercise: «The ring had a ruby set in gold.» What is a ruby? | A small bird | *A precious stone, often cut to shine | A kind of fruit | A metal used for pans
exercise: Mum says, «Grandma is a real jewel.» What does jewel mean here? | A piece of jewellery | A stone dug out of a mine | A shiny coin | *Someone very special and valuable
exercise: «The pirates hid the jewels in a chest full of gold.» What are the jewels? | *Precious stones, such as diamonds or rubies | Old, empty bottles | Wooden toys | Sand and small shells
test: «Jewel in the crown» means what? | A piece of jewellery | A rock with no shine | *The best part of something | A crown made of gold
test: Which of these is a gemstone dug out of the ground? | A plastic bead | A grain of sand | *An emerald | A plain pebble
exam: Read: «She is a real jewel.» Which is the best explanation? | She is hidden in a treasure chest | She is a piece of jewellery | *She is very special and valuable | She is made of precious stone
